descriptions.job-059my0t:
&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Payouts and FX team helps global businesses manage their money wherever it flows. We own Stripe&#39;s FX and multi-currency management products—including FX Acquiring, Multicurrency Settlement (MCS), and Currency Conversion—which together serve tens of thousands of global merchants and platforms. Our team works at the intersection of payments, treasury, and financial infrastructure, helping businesses reduce FX costs, eliminate third-party dependencies, and consolidate their multi-currency operations onto Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will own the full commercial cycle—prospecting, structuring, closing, and activating deals—across Stripe&#39;s FX Acquiring, Multicurrency Settlement (MCS), and Currency Conversion (ICC) products. You will engage CFO- and Treasurer-level stakeholders at global merchants and platforms, positioning Stripe&#39;s multi-currency suite as the complete alternative to standalone FX management providers. You will also serve as a product specialist for the broader Account Executive team, building the playbooks, deal structures, and GTM motion that scale this business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own quota and commercial responsibility across FX Acquiring, Multicurrency Settlement, and Currency Conversion, prospecting and closing deals with global merchants and platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Structure and negotiate holistic multi-currency deals that bundle MCS and Currency Conversion, pricing across both products to deliver merchant value while capturing the full multi-currency management relationship for Stripe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage C-suite and treasury stakeholders—including CFOs, Treasurers, and Engineering leaders—to articulate Stripe&#39;s multi-currency value proposition and displace competitors managing FX flows off-platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the FX and multi-currency GTM product specialist for the broader Account Executive team, partnering on complex deals and helping build repeatable sales motions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and execute go-to-market strategies for new product segments, including pitch frameworks, displacement playbooks, and bundled pricing approaches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate cross-functionally with product, treasury, and core account teams to support merchant activation, resolve deal blockers, and feed market intelligence back into product development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of quota-carrying B2B sales experience in payments, fintech, or financial infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated knowledge of FX and treasury concepts across multiple geographies, including currency risk, settlement mechanics, and cross-border payment flows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing complex, multi-stakeholder sales cycles involving finance and engineering leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of consultative, product-led selling with demonstrated competitive displacement wins&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building a go-to-market motion for a new product or market segment, from initial targeting through to scaled execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with multi-currency account products, FX management platforms, or global treasury tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

descriptions.job-1xhupa5:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Product Sales is a team of functional and technical specialists who both lead and advise on deals for the most strategically important products in Stripe’s portfolio. Revenue suite Product Sales is tasked with attacking a $100B market opportunity for back office finance automation across billing, tax, revenue reporting, and data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Billing Account Executive at Stripe, you&#39;ll use your sales and product expertise to help drive growth through both existing and new-to-Stripe customers. You&#39;ll collaborate with the core sales, marketing, product marketing, and product teams to develop deep product and industry knowledge and drive strategic deals. You&#39;ll lead in-depth product discussions with existing and prospective customers and build and execute against our go-to-market strategy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive revenue to achieve and overperform on targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead new sales and upsell conversations of Stripe for existing and prospective customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive strategic thought leadership within assigned territory to ensure user success and revenue growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand the sales process and competitors for Stripe, including software, hardware, and payments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as both an internal and customer-facing expert on Stripe, especially for your specialized products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Synthesize and relay customer feedback and our findings to inform Stripe&#39;s product roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage with Product, Marketing, and User Operations teams to help amplify our growth trajectory&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;You&#39;re an adept salesperson, capable of engaging in business-level and technical conversations at multiple levels of the organization, including CEO, CFO, and CTO. You&#39;re used to building value in competitive situations and enjoy working on products that require deep product understanding, combined with technical knowledge. You&#39;re as comfortable working with clients as with internal stakeholders (including executives). You&#39;re excited to become an expert and to share your knowledge. You&#39;re an organized self-starter, an excellent communicator who is detail-oriented and has a track record for improving the processes and organizations around you.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of sales or prospecting experience at a technology company and a track record of top performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owning a direct sales quota, with direct sales experience closing new business and expanding existing users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven ability to build strong collaborative working relationships with business partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to deal with ambiguity and thrive in an unstructured, fast-moving environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven ability to be a self-starter capable of driving business results without significant supervision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A hands-on mentality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent verbal and written communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong presentation skills, particularly for in-person meetings with multiple stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead complex negotiations involving bespoke commercial agreements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand complex technical requirements and craft solutions across multiple stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience selling financial services or similar software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in selling billing solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to sell in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

descriptions.job-0091ldp:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is looking for a senior product strategist-operator to support the Risk team. Risk is central to Stripe’s ability to grow safely: the team protects Stripe and our users while enabling durable, responsible growth. In this role, you will have a front-row seat to high-stakes business and product decisions and a direct hand in helping the team identify emerging risks, prioritize the right interventions, and deliver measurable outcomes. If you are a technical strategist who moves quickly, brings clarity to ambiguity, and stays with difficult problems through resolution, we’d love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will partner closely with Risk leaders and cross-functional teams across Product, Engineering, Data Science, Finance, Operations, and Strategy. You will create strategic clarity around Risk’s performance, connect business and product signals, pressure-test plans, and mobilize teams when results are off track. The role combines rigorous analysis with hands-on execution: you will not only identify where Stripe should act, but also help drive the work required to change the trajectory.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for someone who can connect risk signals, data, financial performance, user impact, and product and business strategy. You can find the signal in the noise, form a clear point of view, and either address the problem directly or convene the right people to solve it quickly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will work across Risk and Stripe’s technical and user-facing teams to improve decision-making, strengthen execution, and help Stripe manage risk while serving users well.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the signal: Define and maintain the metrics that matter for Risk’s in-year performance, spanning risk outcomes, business impact, operational health, and user experience. Build a disciplined “morning read”—a curated, high-signal view that surfaces emerging issues and drives timely action beyond standard dashboarding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead deep-dive interventions: Run focused “surge” efforts to diagnose and unblock critical goals at risk. Move from symptom to root cause, align teams on the response, and stay engaged until the trajectory has measurably improved.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bridge Risk, Product, and Strategy: Translate long-horizon company and risk theses into in-year priorities and operating plans. Decompose ambiguous opportunities and threats that cut across Product, Risk, Operations, and go-to-market teams into structured workstreams with clear owners and outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Synthesize for leadership: Anticipate the questions senior leaders will ask and prepare clear, decision-oriented materials that turn complex and unstructured risk signals into diagnoses, options, and recommended actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pressure-test assumptions: Work closely with Risk, Corporate Strategy, Product, and Finance to test whether plans reflect external market dynamics, changing risk patterns, user needs, and Stripe’s execution capacity. Identify gaps early and help teams adapt.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of experience in product strategy, business operations, data analytics, product management, or strategic business performance roles, ideally in high-growth technology companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in product strategy, product management, or GM-style roles with direct ownership of a P&amp;amp;L or a specific business outcome&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deeply curious about business models and data, probing into signals, understanding trends and customer usage patterns to uncover novel insights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven track record of directly driving business growth through analytical insights and execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to apply AI to improve decision-making and operational efficiency, with sound judgment about when and how to use AI tools without sacrificing rigor or quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product sense and the ability to understand the technical mechanics of how software products are built and scaled&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience navigating ambiguous, cross-functional problems and leading high-stakes interventions with senior stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience with fintech products or complex financial systems is a plus, but not required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience facilitating senior leadership and stakeholder discussions that lead to clear decisions and action on business performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in risk, payments, financial services, or fintech&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to build trust and partner with senior leaders and CXOs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical proficiency in SQL / Python / R and data analysis; ability to self-serve and perform independent deep-dives into complex datasets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing creative solutions and influencing the roadmaps of cross-functional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to anticipate how product launches, policy changes, and go-to-market activity affect risk outcomes, user experience, and support operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

descriptions.job-0zir4l9:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Company&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded by CPAs, tax attorneys, and engineers, Taxbit is the leading innovator automating global tax reporting for the digital economy. Taxbit&#39;s AI-enabled platform streamlines compliance related to digital assets, payments, and other financial transactions. Its unique combination of deep subject matter expertise and AI-forward technology have made it a fast-growing disruptor trusted by the world&#39;s leading fintechs, marketplaces, digital asset players, Big 4 accounting firms, traditional enterprises, and government agencies. Backed by top-tier Silicon Valley VCs, Taxbit&#39;s team is located across offices in San Francisco, New York, Seattle, Salt Lake City, London, Madrid, and Singapore.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Opportunity for Impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;TaxBit is looking for a Staff Software Engineer to join our Systems, Security &amp;amp; Compliance organization and take ownership of the cloud infrastructure that powers our platform. In this role, you will be a technical leader for our AWS environment, driving the architecture, automation, and operational excellence of systems that our customers and internal teams depend on. You will also help shape and drive our AI (Dev)Ops strategy, defining how we deploy, monitor, and operate AI-enabled systems responsibly and at scale. You will have broad influence over how we build, deploy, secure, and monitor infrastructure at scale, partnering closely with engineering, security, and compliance stakeholders to raise the bar on reliability, security, and developer velocity across the company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role and Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and operate secure, highly available cloud infrastructure on AWS supporting TaxBit&#39;s platform and products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own infrastructure-as-code using AWS CDK (preferred) or Terraform, driving consistency, repeatability, and version control across environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, maintain, and continuously improve CI/CD pipelines (GitHub/GitHub Actions) to enable safe, frequent, and reliable deployments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and implement TaxBit&#39;s backup and disaster recovery strategy across cloud data stores and critical systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect and evolve data storage and processing patterns that support scalability, reliability, and cost efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement and maintain centralized logging, monitoring, and observability across services and infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement and maintain security guardrails integrated throughout the development lifecycle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build workflow automation that reduces manual toil in infrastructure provisioning, deployments, and operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Debug and resolve complex issues across distributed, cloud-native systems, driving root-cause analysis and durable fixes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement AI Ops/AI DevOps practices to deploy, monitor, and operate AI-enabled systems and pipelines in production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally with engineering, security, and compliance teams using tools such as GitHub, Linear/Jira, and Databricks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Professional Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree (B.Sc. minimum) in Computer Science or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant experience in systems/infrastructure engineering, with deep, hands-on expertise in AWS cloud infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong programming skills in Python, TypeScript, or an equivalent language&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Required: hands-on experience with CI/CD, GitHub, and Infrastructure-as-Code (AWS CDK preferred, Terraform acceptable)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing and implementing backup strategy, data architecture, and disaster recovery for cloud systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience implementing and maintaining logging and monitoring/observability solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Security-minded, with experience implementing and maintaining security guardrails in engineering workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with workflow automation and strong debugging skills across distributed systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with collaboration and workflow tooling such as Linear/Jira and Databricks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with AI governance practices and frameworks (e.g., ISO 42001) for managing AI systems responsibly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of AI security risks and mitigations (e.g., model/data access controls, prompt injection, secure use of AI tooling)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Personal Characteristics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Security-minded by default, with a proactive approach to identifying and mitigating risk&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong sense of ownership and accountability for systems end to end&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communicator who collaborates effectively across engineering, security, and compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable operating with autonomy in a fast-paced, high-growth environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pragmatic problem-solver who balances speed with reliability and security&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Acts as an enabler for other engineers, building platforms, tools, and guardrails that make it easier for teams to ship safely and quickly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative by nature, building strong working relationships across engineering, security, and compliance to get to the best outcome together&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Compensation &amp;amp; Benefits&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base salary range for this role is $170,000-$250,000. Certain roles may be eligible for incentive compensation, equity, and benefits. Actual compensation will vary depending on various job-related factors, including, but not limited to location, experience, level, and job qualifications.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits &amp;amp; Perks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive cash compensation (based on experience)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equity (RSUs)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive benefits package&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A modern 401(k) plan that includes access to crypto, financial wellness benefits, low fees and more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hybrid working model: 3 days in-office, 2 days WFH/flexible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monday team lunches, snacks and drinks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Discretionary Time Off - enjoy the flexibility to rest, refuel, and recharge&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid parental leave to bond with your child&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fertility Benefit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Autonomous work and flexibility in how work is performed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Taxbit in the News&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
